														<h3 class="factitle">Pedagogy &amp; Experiential Learning</h3>

														<ul class="facul">
															<li>Behavioural case studies, structured role plays (conflict resolution, negotiation, appraisal and feedback conversations, selection interviews), and people-management simulations integrated across the curriculum.</li>

															<li>Psychometric and self-assessment instruments (Big Five, Emotional Intelligence, MBTI-style type indicators, FIRO-B, conflict-mode inventories) debriefed through guided reflection to build genuine self-awareness.</li>

															<li>Experiential labs — group-dynamics exercises, fishbowl discussions, in-basket and assessment-centre activities, and sensitivity/T-group–style sessions.</li>

															<li>Live HR projects: competency mapping, employee-engagement surveys, and the design of performance-appraisal and reward systems for partner organisations.</li>

															<li>Continuous assessment via reflective learning journals, peer feedback, behavioural observation, and HR live-case presentations.</li>

															<li>Assessment through Filed Projects.</li>
														</ul>

														<h3 class="factitle">Technology Integration in the Classroom</h3>

														<ul class="facul">
															<li>Hands-on exposure to People Analytics dashboards.</li>

															<li>Active use of AI and Generative AI for HR workflows — drafting JDs and policies, examining resume-screening logic and its bias risks, designing L&amp;D content, and building interview banks.</li>

															<li>People-analytics and data-visualisation tools to interpret attrition, engagement, and performance data.</li>
														</ul>
